{"name":"Azul Tequila","hex":"#c0cfc7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tequila","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic liquor distilled from the fermented juice of the Central American century plant Agave tequilana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tequila"}],"entries":[{"title":"Azul Tequila","blocks":[{"text":"Azul Tequila is a Mexican telenovela. The 160-episode serial was produced for TV Azteca by the celebrity couple Christian Bach and Humberto Zurita in conjunction with Humberto's brother Gerardo through their production company ZUBA Producciones. The complete series has been released in an 8 DVD box set."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9c/Azul_Tequila_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azul_Tequila","wikidata":"Q6392059"},{"title":"Tequila","blocks":[{"text":"Tequila is a distilled beverage made from the blue agave plant, primarily in the area surrounding the town of Tequila 65 km (40 mi) northwest of Guadalajara, and in the Jaliscan Highlands of the central western Mexican state of Jalisco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Paisaje_agavero_de_Jose_Cuervo_en_Tequila%2C_Jalisco.jpg/330px-Paisaje_agavero_de_Jose_Cuervo_en_Tequila%2C_Jalisco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tequila","wikidata":"Q122195"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tequila_oven.jpg/500px-Tequila_oven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tequila_oven.jpg/1280px-Tequila_oven.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Tequila_oven.jpg/500px-Tequila_oven.jpg?utm_source=en